{
  "_readme": [
    "The ten approved palettes \u2014 the ONE place they are defined. build.mjs reads this file, writes the matching",
    "rules into theme.css (between the @PALETTES markers) and the swatches on the page, and checks contrast.",
    "Each palette: id (two digits, keep stable \u2014 saved meetings point at it), name, light = [primary, secondary, tertiary]",
    "as hex for a white surface, and optional dark = the same three for the dark surface. Leave dark out and the build",
    "derives it by lifting the light values (hue and saturation kept). The build fails loudly if a light value falls",
    "below 4.5:1 as text on #F1F2F5 or a dark value below 6:1 on #171B22 \u2014 fix the hex, or say --allow-low-contrast.",
    "After editing: node scripts/build.mjs --out prebuilt --minify --emit-md references  (then delete prebuilt/build-info.json),",
    "update the table in references/palettes.md, and republish."
  ],
